{"name":"Deconstruction","hex":"#7b736b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deconstruction","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A philosophical theory of textual criticism; a form of critical analysis that emphasizes inquiry into the variable projection of the meaning and message of critical works, the meaning in relation to the reader and the intended audience, and the assumptions implicit in the embodied forms of expression.","The destroying or taking apart of an object; disassembly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deconstruction"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deconstruction","blocks":[{"text":"In philosophy, deconstruction is a loosely defined set of approaches to understanding the relationship between text and meaning. The concept of deconstruction was introduced by the philosopher Jacques Derrida, who described it as a turn away from Platonism's ideas of \"true\" forms and essences which are valued above appearances. American literary critic and major proponent of deconstruction Barbara Johnson describes the approach in this way:"},{"text":"The deconstruction of a text does not proceed by random doubt or generalized skepticism, but by the careful teasing out of warring forces of signification within the text itself."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deconstruction"},{"title":"Deconstruction (Devin Townsend Project album)","blocks":[{"text":"Deconstruction is the thirteenth studio album by Canadian musician Devin Townsend, and the third album in the Devin Townsend Project series. The album was released on June 20, 2011, simultaneously with the fourth Devin Townsend Project album Ghost, on Townsend's independent record label HevyDevy Records. The album features two drummers, Dirk Verbeuren and Ryan Van Poederooyen, as well as a number of guest vocalists. The album's choral and orchestral parts were written and arranged by Townsend using Pro Tools software. The parts were later transcribed into conventional musical notation for the orchestra."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Deconstruction_%28The_Devin_Townsend_Project_album%29_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deconstruction_(Devin_Townsend_Project_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/JudithButler2013.jpg/500px-JudithButler2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/JudithButler2013.jpg/500px-JudithButler2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Judith Butler","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJudithButler2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/Decon_Slipcase.jpeg/250px-Decon_Slipcase.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Decon_Slipcase.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/Decon_Slipcase.jpeg/250px-Decon_Slipcase.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADecon_Slipcase.jpeg"}],"sounds":{"deconstruction":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-deconstruction.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/04/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-deconstruction.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-deconstruction.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/04/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-deconstruction.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-deconstruction.wav.ogg"}]}